<div style="font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px;">
  <h1 style="font-size: 20px;">Your sign-in link</h1>
  <p>Someone (hopefully you) asked to sign in as <strong><%= user.email %></strong>.</p>
  <p style="margin: 24px 0;">
    <a href="<%= sign_in_url %>"
       style="background: #4f46e5; color: #fff; padding: 10px 18px; border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none;">
      Sign in
    </a>
  </p>
  <p style="color: #666; font-size: 13px;">
    The link works once, for <%= minutes %> minutes, in the browser that asked for it.
    If you didn't request this, you can ignore this email.
  </p>
</div>
